invalid type: string "to your .bashrc: export GITPS1SHOWDIRTYSTATE=1 export PS1='\\w$(_gitps1 \" (%s)\")\\$ ' The \\w means print the current working directory, the \\$ prints the $ part of the prompt, and _gitps1 \" (%s)\" basically says to make the topic branch on the remote nothing, which deletes it. Or you can use the newer syntax (available since Git v1.7.0): $ git push origin --delete topic/